The Gemini model list now matches Google's current models page, and the commit is 2158429e ("Fixes #1118"). Formatting, clippy with warnings as errors, the build and the full test suite all pass.

The issue was partly fixed already. I checked the list again before editing. The two ids #1118 named, gemini-3.0-pro and gemini-3.0-flash, were no longer offered. What was still wrong:
• gemini-2.0-flash was still on the google list, which hid it from the "Unknown model" warning, but Google marks it "Shut down".
• Current ids were missing, so the warning's list of known models showed deprecated 2.5 ids first.

How I checked: I compared every Gemini id yoyo offers against Google's models page and each id's own page (read 2026-11-08), and against yoagent 0.27.4's presets and price table. The full table is in the commit body.
• Added: gemini-3.6-flash and gemini-3.1-pro-preview (both have yoagent presets), plus gemini-3.5-flash-lite, gemini-3.1-flash-lite and gemini-3-flash-preview (on Google's page, no preset).
• Kept: gemini-2.5-flash-lite, which Google says is "not deprecated". Also gemini-2.5-pro and gemini-2.5-flash: deprecated and closed to new users, but still served to existing ones until they are rerouted on 2026-12-01. The dated source is in the test table.
• Dropped: gemini-2.0-flash. It and the two 3.0 ids are now in the list of ids no vendor serves, so adding one back fails a test.
• Not added: gemini-3.5-flash and 3.7-flash. The issue named them, but they are no longer on Google's page.
• Unchanged: the default is still gemini-3.8-flash, and Google still lists it.

Files changed:
• src/providers.rs: the google list now puts current ids first and drops 2.0-flash. It also has the new test every_offered_gemini_id_is_a_yoagent_preset_or_on_googles_page. Every Gemini id offered must be known to yoagent or listed in a table that cites Google's page. The test also fails if a cited id later gets a yoagent preset, or if nothing offers it. It checks that every offered id reports a 1,048,576-token window, the figure on each id's Google page.
• src/commands.rs: the /model completion list gains the two preset ids.
• src/commands_info.rs: the pinned window for Gemini 2.0 is gone, and the Gemini 3.x and 2.5 windows now cite Google's pages instead of saying "estimated".
• docs/src/configuration/models.md: the example uses gemini-3.1-pro-preview, and the list of ids running on guessed limits names the newly offered ones.
• tests/module_size.rs: line counts updated. commands.rs is +10 lines, 2 of them from this change and 8 from earlier unrecorded growth; commands_info.rs is −5.

Checks:
• Sabotage check: I put gemini-3.0-pro back on the list with the marker, ran the test and restored the file in one command. The test failed by name ("google offers gemini-3.0-pro: no yoagent preset/price row…"), then passed once restored.
• Running the binary: --model gemini-3.0-pro prints the "Unknown model" warning, and gemini-3.5-flash-lite doesn't. Ids without a preset still get the separate guessed-limits note. At first I thought that note was missing, but my search was for warning and the note starts with ⚠; the commit body has the corrected output.

I found no dead non-Gemini ids, so I posted nothing on #1147, and nothing in the repo links to #1118.
